= The eval server: heap, pool sized by memory, sweep, and the docs
The server gets an 8g heap, the harness waits for its token instead of
sleeping a second, and evalserver-sweep.raku runs a directory in chunks
across a pool sized against MemAvailable (jobs x heap, --force to go
over). The eval client is Raku; RakOps' rv-decont site cache resets per
run; the sweep forces RAKUDO_RAKUAST=1 and unbuffers its progress.
docs/jvm-eval-server.md and docs/jvm-newdisp-port.md are written.
- b7eeeab9db Give the eval server a heap, a start worth waiting for, and a sweep
- 69206c0f09 Size the eval server pool by memory, and speak Raku to it
- c58448ab8e JVM: clear the rv-decont sites per eval-server run, and document it all
- 03e26859cb JVM has no 16-bit argument limit, and the sweep must not forget its frontend
- 1b51112e14 Document the JVM newdisp port's true state, and unbuffer sweep progress

= Unify static-code identity for BEGIN-bound code on the JVM
A BEGIN-time dynamic compilation bound code objects to the nested
unit's code refs while the enclosing unit emitted the same cuids anew,
splitting the lexical universe a begin-created phaser closes over from
the one the runtime executes; the comp unit now emits a load-time
jvm-repoint-dynamic-code fixup for those cuids. The port doc records the
root cause and resolution, and AGENTS.md is born as the session-start
briefing (CLAUDE.md symlinks to it).
- 66eabbd824 Root-cause the traited-variable failure to static-code identity
- 0a8dd95a8b Give agents a session-start briefing that survives anything
- ba94206b9a Unify static-code identity for BEGIN-bound code on the JVM

