= RakuAST: fuse \r\n across a WithWhitespace wrapper
IMPL-FUSE-CRLF looks through the WithWhitespace wrapper an atom with
trailing whitespace arrives in, so `/ ^ \r\n $ /` fuses like `/^\r\n$/`.
The grapheme-position assertion in regex-crlf-grapheme.t is skipped on
the JVM with its reason: .from/.to are char indices without NFG strings.
- 8bc2c1fc94 Skip the grapheme-position assertion on the JVM
- ac965414c7 RakuAST: fuse \r\n across a WithWhitespace wrapper

= make j-spectest on one warm eval server; leak-check and hprof tooling
The jvm harness passes --evalserver, so a spectest runs through one
warm server (full spectest ~2h20m through an 8g server). evalserver-
leak-check.sh pushes rounds of files through a server and prints live
GlobalContext counts; hprof_extract.py and hprof_paths.py find shortest
paths from a class's instances to GC roots in a heap dump. The
eval-server doc gains the post-mortem.
